        "selector": {
          "type": "FragmentSelector",
          "value": "xywh=pixel:71,11,331,182",
          "conformsTo": "http://www.w3.org/TR/media-frags/"
        }
      },
      "body": [
        {
          "type": "TextualBody",
          "value": "\n<ol><li>[&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;] in this document. The named sellers collected</li>\n<li>in full and completely. And [the sellers] released him (the buyer) by means of a receipt (acknowledging that they have) received and taken (the price) over fully. They delivered (the property) to him</li>\n<li>And he owned it and acquired it and it passed into his possession and into his holding as his property.</li>\n<li>He has the same freedom of choice with regard to it that owners customarily have with regard to their property. [&hellip;.] (in this sale there is) no claim,</li>\n<li>exception, nor any condition after this. And this is after their understanding and investigation of everything that [&hellip;&hellip;]</li>\n<li>The execution of all claims should there be any claims made by a third party or by way of attachments made against the named buyer regarding all that he has bought, made by any</li>\n<li>person, is obligatory upon her, and not on the buyers whose name has been mentioned, from her own money</li>\n<li>whatever it may be. (This sale has been performed) according to the condition of the sale of Islam and its contract. Witnesses testified to the acknowledgement by the</li>\n<li>mentioned seller of the sale [ and receipt of the price and the acknowledgement by] the buyer of the acquirement (of the property).</li>\n<li>They came to know them in person and by their names. (This was) after the whole document was read to all of them, letter by letter</li>\n<li>from its beginning to its end and they understood it and acknowledged that they have understood it being in sound mind and body,</li>\n<li>legally capable of conducting their affairs, acting voluntarily, not forced or coerced. This was written in the beginning of Sha&rsquo;b\u0101n</li>\n<li>of the year four hundred and fifty-four.</li></ol>\n",
          "format": "text/html"
        }
      ],
      "motivation": [
        "sc:supplementing",
        "translating"
      ],
      "schema:position": 1
    },
    {
